    <other_details id="References">Archetypes: openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-ROLE.generic_role.v1, openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.electronic_communication.v1. Derived from the CKM drafts openEHR-DEMOGRAPHIC-ROLE.individual_provider.v0 and CAPABILITY.individual_credentials.v0. Aligned with the HL7 FHIR R4 (4.0.1) resource PractitionerRole (https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/).</other_details>
    <details>
      <language>
        <terminology_id>
          <value>ISO_639-1</value>
        </terminology_id>
        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>A function that actors perform, such as care provider, patient or administrator, with its capabilities and its contacts.</purpose>
      <keywords>role</keywords>
      <keywords>function</keywords>
      <keywords>capability</keywords>
      <keywords>permission</keywords>
      <use>Use for a role in a demographic service. Where a service keeps one ROLE per function, actors hold it through a role assignment relationship of their own; the ROLE then holds no relationships.</use>
      <misuse>Not for a person's qualifications or registrations: record those on the person.</misuse>
      <copyright>© openehr-reference-content contributors</copyright>
    </details>
  </description>
